    50	## Rulings in this plan (for the user's review)
    51	
    52	- **Carriers replace type-class facets.** Phase 0 deviation (d) made a facet a type class over `Instance`. A claim `∀ I [HasStrong I], …` is vacuous for an instance without the class, and two class instances can attach to one `I` (PHASE0-REPORT §6, Facet row). In this plan a facet is a structure that extends `Instance` (`StrongInstance`), so the facet value is a field and is bound once. A claim that needs the facet is a `ClaimSpec Carrier.strong`: only a `StrongInstance` can hold a certificate of it. A new facet is an addition: a new structure, its carrier and a `CarrierMap` to v1. Existing claims and certificates pull back through the map (G2). Deviation (d) is superseded.
    53	- **The same carrier generalizes the engine (I5).** A claim quantifies over `K.Ctx I W` (for v1: an environment and a v1 run). Engine v2 (plan 2) adds a new carrier value. It does not change `ClaimSpec`.
    54	- **`ProtocolParams` stays inside the protocol.** A protocol value is built from its parameters (`sapc p`), so `Instance` gets no `pparams` field. Profile constants (`Shared`) are the shared constants of design §3–§4 (deviation (g)). If wrong: a later field, which is an addition.
    55	- **`Instance` gets `Δ_pos : 0 < Δ`.** Without it an instance with `Δ ≤ 0` has no admissible context, and every `holds` is vacuous. `Cert.inhabited` already rejects such an instance, but the equivalence theorems (Task 9) need the field.
    56	- **One lock regeneration.** Tasks 1–4 break `docs/catalog.lock` on purpose. Task 6 hardens the lock script and writes the new lock ONCE, with a dated entry in the design's §8 lock change log. Approval of this plan is the user's approval of that regeneration, as for the receipt-relay lock rewrite (`0dd5993`).
    57	- **The I1 gap becomes a compiled witness, not a fix.** Task 5 proves that a protocol that reads no input (`clockChain`) is a `Candidate`. The fix needs engine v2 (plan 2). The witness lives in `AvailableChainRegistry/Gaps/`, and the registry marks its rows `KNOWN-GAP`, not `LEAN`.
    58	- **HooksSound stays run-level** (deviation (i)); `deps_stable` has the same shape as `processed_stable`.
    59	
    60	## Global Constraints
    61	
    62	- Toolchain and Mathlib v4.30.0-rc2. Do not run `lake update`.
    63	- Committed proofs use no `sorry`, no `admit`, no project axioms and no `native_decide`. A `sorry` is allowed only between a task's statement step and its CHECKPOINT. `lake build --wfail` fails on every `sorry`. `scripts/Registry.lean` rejects every axiom outside `propext`, `Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound` in a certificate row.
    64	- Work on `main` in `lean/available-chain` (user decision 2026-09-28: commit the work frequently). Commit only the task's files, by explicit path, with a message `Framework: <task title>`. Never stage `log.md`, `state.md`, `docs/FG-COMPOSITION.md`, or any file of `AvailableChainSimplexFG`, `AvailableChainKitFG`, or the FG scripts.
    65	- Do not change `AvailableChainModel`, `AvailableChainStatements`, `AvailableChainGridCO`, `AvailableChainSA`, `AvailableChainSAPC`, `AvailableChainLStar` or `AvailableChainWitnesses`. `AvailableChainRegistry/GridCOHooks.lean` is in the registry and changes in Task 3.
    66	- Layer rule (design §1): `AvailableChainFramework` modules other than `Kit/` import nothing from `AvailableChainRegistry` or `Kit/`. Catalog helper lemmas that a `transport` proof needs go in `AvailableChainFramework/Catalog/Mono.lean` (L3), not in `Kit/`.
    67	- Builds. During the work: `lake build --wfail AvailableChainFramework AvailableChainRegistry`. At the end (Task 10): the full `lake build --wfail`. The Mac `lean` has 3 machine-wide slots: run `pgrep -fl lean` before a build and wait if 3 compiles run. Scripts run with `lake env lean --run <file>`, never through a `lean_exe`.
    68	- Lock and registry during the gate. `lake env lean --run scripts/CatalogLock.lean --check` exits 1 from Task 1 until Task 6. This is expected. From Task 6 on, it must exit 0 at every CHECKPOINT (the hardened script exits 0 on additions only). `lake env lean --run scripts/Registry.lean` must run at every CHECKPOINT from Task 1 on (Task 1 updates it for the new `Cert` arity).
    69	- `Time` is `abbrev Time := Int` in another module. `omega` does not unfold it in this toolchain: use `linarith`, `Int` order lemmas, or an explicit `(x : Int)` cast (PHASE0-REPORT §5.2, Tasks 4 and 9).
    70	- Root imports. A task that creates a `.lean` file adds `public import <module>` for it to its library root (`AvailableChainFramework.lean` or `AvailableChainRegistry.lean`) in the same commit.
    71	- Each task ends at a CHECKPOINT: the build is green; the registry script runs; the lock check has the result that this section states; the task is committed.
    72	- Prose in comments and docs: ASD-STE100 Simplified Technical English. Tables: Unicode box drawing in fenced `text` blocks.
