   511	- [ ] **Step 3: The four certificates and the candidate.** At `D = 0`.
   512	  - Safety of both outputs: in a run, the state of a node after its events up to `t` is the time of its last tick at or before `t` (or `0`). Every read is `clockBlock m` for some `m`; `clockBlock a ⪯ clockBlock b` when `a ≤ b`, so reads agree; the last-tick time is monotone in `t`.
   513	  - Prefix: the two outputs are equal.
   514	  - Inclusion at `D = 0`: for a slot `s` with `0 < s`, an honest awake proposer ticks at `s` (`tick_total`; `s` is public with `Δ = 1`), emits `⟨.proposer s, s⟩`, and `block s = clockBlock s`. Every honest node ticks at `s`, so its read at `s` is `clockBlock s`.
   515	  - Inhabitation: a one-validator run with a tick at every integer time `0 … N` and no delivery, as `AvailableChainWitnesses/Sanity.lean` (`exampleRun`, `exampleExecution`, `exampleSynchrony`, `exampleRootInjective`, `exampleSleepy`). `PartialSynchrony` holds because `excludes` is always true and nothing is accepted. `RootInjective`: the roots of `clockBlock k` are `⟨k⟩`. For the late inclusion trigger, take the slot `max H 1` (as a natural number) and a horizon of at least that slot.
   516	  - `clockCandidate : Candidate clockInst` with `shared := 0`.
